        "original_id": "36802bb3-019b-5819-9d7e-920cd6ce5bef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Columbian Iron Works and Dry Dock Company\n- Places: Baltimore, Maryland; Locust Point peninsula; Fort McHenry; Baltimore Harbor; Chesapeake Bay\n- Events: War of 1812; British attack on Baltimore Harbor\n- Concepts: coastal pentagonal bastion fort\n\nFacts:\n- On September 13–14, 1814, Fort McHenry successfully defended Baltimore Harbor in Baltimore, Maryland from an attack by the British navy from the Chesapeake Bay during the War of 1812.\n- Fort McHenry is a historical American coastal pentagonal bastion fort in Baltimore, Maryland.\n- From 1872 to 1899, the Columbian Iron Works and Dry Dock Company was located in Baltimore, Maryland on the Locust Point peninsula adjacent to Fort McHenry.",
